# Five-paper bridge checks (S14, 2026-10-06)

## A. The Collatz backward tree never splits completely (Golod-Shafarevich bridge)

Compressed map T(x) = x/2 (x even), (3x+1)/2 (x odd); preimages of y: 2y always, (2y-1)/3 iff y = 2 mod 3.
PROVED (congruence): if y = 2 mod 3 then 2y = 1 mod 3, so the even child of a branching vertex never branches;
hence no vertex has a complete binary backward subtree of depth 2, and no 'section splits completely at every level'.
FINITE-EXACT: maximal complete-splitting depth over all starts below 10^5 = 1.
Backward layer sizes from 8, depth 0..40: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 12, 18, 24, 31, 39, 50, 68, 91, 120, 159, 211, 282, 381, 505, 665, 885, 1187, 1590, 2122, 2829, 3765, 5014, 6682, 8902, 11878, 15844, 21122, 28150, 37536, 50067, 66763, 89009, 118631, 158171]
Successive ratios at depth 30..40: [1.3343, 1.3339, 1.3331, 1.3327, 1.3334, 1.3338, 1.3335, 1.3332, 1.3328, 1.3333] (mean branching 1 + P(y = 2 mod 3) = 4/3 = 1.3333)

## B. Near-zero-sum reading of the gate crossings (3SUM / Exact-Triangle bridge)

A k-step word w with sum s closes a cycle iff (2^s - 3^k) y = c_w exactly (an exact zero sum of the two ledgers plus
the correction); a gate crossing is an approximate zero sum: y < c_w/(2^s - 3^k).  Margin 2^(t_k)/3^k - 1 and gate
radius R_k = c_max/(2^(t_k) - 3^k), c_max = 3^(k-1) + 2^(t_k-k+1)(3^(k-1) - 2^(k-1)), for the lags with margin < 0.06:
  k= 5 t_k=  8 margin=0.0535 R_k=86.2  (none: no lattice point below the gate)
  k=17 t_k= 27 margin=0.0393 R_k=17344.6  (12 exceptions)
  k=29 t_k= 46 margin=0.0253 R_k=3449770.4  (56)
  k=41 t_k= 65 margin=0.0115 R_k=970158188.7  (62)
The small-margin lags below 45 are exactly 5, 17, 29, 41 (the upper semiconvergents 8/5, 27/17, 46/29, 65/41 of log2 3);
exceptions exist at 17, 29, 41 and not at 5, so the margin is necessary and the cylinder offset decides (S13).

