  -> at m = 18 the plus sheet gains exactly 11 non-generic chord patterns (only 437's actual pattern is word-realisable).
  minus sheet x=165 word [1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 5, 1, 1, 1]: differing chord [(0, 12)] (sum 19 = t_12); realisable: True
  minus sheet x=309 word [1, 2, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1]: differing chord [(0, 12)] (sum 19 = t_12); realisable: False
  minus sheet x=549 word [1, 2, 1, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1]: differing chord [(0, 12)] (sum 19 = t_12); realisable: True
  -> at m = 13 the minus sheet gains exactly 1 non-generic pattern (309's).
In every crossing only the long chord (0, m-1) separates from the word prediction: the pinch is the single gate of the
whole window, and the sub-windows are generic (short-lag genericity).

ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED
